  "Question": "The average age of the \\(6\\) people in Room A is \\(40.\\) The average age of the \\(4\\) people in Room B is \\(25.\\) If the two groups are combined, what is the average age of all the people?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( \\ 32.5 \\)",
    "B": "\\( \\ 33 \\)",
    "C": "\\( \\ 33.5 \\)",
    "D": "\\( \\ 34 \\)",
    "E": "\\( \\ 35 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "To combine the groups, first find their total ages. Room A contributes \\(6\\times40=240\\) years, and Room B contributes \\(4\\times25=100\\) years. The group sizes matter because each room's average represents a different number of people.\n\nThere are \\(6+4=10\\) people altogether, so their average age is\n\\[\n\\frac{240+100}{10}=34\\text{ years}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(34\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
